# Nuclear branch before PR (non-negotiable)

**Never open or push-for-review a PR until `nuclear-branch` has been run on the
branch (or uncommitted set about to ship) and High findings are fixed or
explicitly waived by the user.**

This is the PR-time gate. Plan-time OpenSpec nuclear is separate — see
`nuclear-openspec-before-implement.mdc`.

## When it applies

- User asks to create a PR (`gh pr create`, “open a PR”, “ship it”)
- User asks to push a branch that is intended for review (first push of a
  feature/fix branch, or push after substantial new commits)
- Agent is about to run `gh pr create` per user request

## Agent workflow

1. Ensure CI gates for commit/push are already satisfied (`ci-before-commit`,
   `integration-before-push` as applicable).
2. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/nuclear-branch/SKILL.md` (triple: review,
   quality, contracts). Prefer Diff `branch changes` vs the PR base.
3. Fix High findings on the branch (new commit(s) + `ci-local` again) **or**
   get an explicit user waiver per finding.
4. Only then `git push` (if needed) and `gh pr create` / update the PR body with
   a short **Nuclear** note: pass / findings fixed / waived.

## PR description

Include a one-liner under Test plan or a **Nuclear** subsection, e.g.:

- `nuclear-branch: pass` 
- `nuclear-branch: fixed N High (…); M Medium deferred`

## Exceptions (narrow)

- User explicitly waives nuclear-branch for this PR (quote in the reply and PR
  body).
- Docs-only / skills-only / chore with no behaviour change — run a **contracts
  skim** (docs/CHANGELOG) and state that full triple was scoped down; do not
  silently skip.
- PR already open and user asks only for a tiny follow-up push: re-run nuclear
  on the **new** commits (or full branch if unsure).

## Never

- Open a PR immediately after commit without nuclear-branch.
- Treat stock plugin `thermos` alone as meeting this gate — use `nuclear-branch`
  (expanded triple including contracts).
- Merge the PR (maintainers only — `no-auto-merge.mdc`).
